meta {
  name: Image - Generate
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/v1/images/generations
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{api_key}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-image",
    "prompt": "A serene Japanese garden with cherry blossoms, koi pond, and stone bridge at sunset",
    "size": "16:9",
    "quality": "high",
    "n": 1
  }
}

docs {
  # Image Generation API

  Generate images using various AI models including Google Gemini, Google Imagen, and Runware models.

  ## Endpoint
  `POST /v1/images/generations`

  ## Authentication
  Required. Use Bearer token authentication with your API key.

  ## Request Body

  ### Required Parameters
  - `model` (string) - Model ID to use (e.g., "google/gemini-2.5-flash-image", "runware/flux-pro-v1.1")
  - `prompt` (string) - Text description of the image to generate (max 4000 characters)

  ### Optional Parameters
  - `size` (string) - Image size/aspect ratio. Can be:
    - Pixel dimensions: "1024x1024", "1792x1024", etc.
    - Aspect ratios: "16:9", "1:1", "9:16", etc. (automatically converted to pixel dimensions)
    - Default: "auto"
  - `quality` (string) - Image quality: "auto", "low", "medium", "high". Default: "auto"
  - `n` (integer) - Number of images to generate (1-16). Default: 1
  - `image` (object | array) - Reference image(s) for image-to-image generation:
    - Single image: `{"data": "base64...", "type": "image/png", "filename": "input.png"}`
    - Multiple images: Array of image objects (max varies by model)
  - `response_format` (string) - "url" (default) or "b64_json"

  ### Supported Image Formats
  - JPEG (image/jpeg, image/jpg)
  - PNG (image/png)
  - GIF (image/gif)
  - WebP (image/webp)
  - BMP (image/bmp)
  - TIFF (image/tiff)
  - ❌ AVIF not supported

  ## Response

  Returns a task ID for async processing:
  ```json
  {
    "taskId": "abc123",
    "status": "pending",
    "type": "image",
    "createdAt": 1234567890,
    "message": "Image generation task created. Use GET /v1/tasks/:taskId to check status."
  }
  ```

  Poll the task status using `GET /v1/tasks/{taskId}` until complete.

  ## Model-Specific Features

  ### Google Gemini Models
  - `google/gemini-2.5-flash-image` - Fast model, max 3 reference images
  - `google/gemini-3-pro-image-preview` - Advanced model, max 14 reference images, supports Google Search grounding

  ### Google Imagen Models
  - `google/imagen-3`, `google/imagen-3-fast`
  - `google/imagen-4`, `google/imagen-4-fast`

  ### Runware Models
  - `runware/flux-pro-v1.1` - FLUX Pro model
  - `runware/bytedance-seedream-v5` - ByteDance Seedream
  - `runware/photomaker` - Subject personalization (requires 1-4 reference images, trigger word "rwre")

  ## Examples

  ### Text-to-Image
  ```json
  {
    "model": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-image",
    "prompt": "A cyberpunk city at night with neon lights",
    "size": "16:9",
    "quality": "high",
    "n": 1
  }
  ```

  ### Image-to-Image (Single Reference)
  ```json
  {
    "model": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-image",
    "prompt": "Transform this into a watercolor painting",
    "image": {
      "data": "base64_encoded_image_data",
      "type": "image/png",
      "filename": "reference.png"
    },
    "size": "1:1"
  }
  ```

  ### Image-to-Image (Multiple References)
  ```json
  {
    "model": "runware/photomaker",
    "prompt": "rwre wearing a professional suit, studio lighting",
    "image": [
      {"data": "base64_1", "type": "image/jpeg"},
      {"data": "base64_2", "type": "image/jpeg"},
      {"data": "base64_3", "type": "image/jpeg"}
    ],
    "size": "1024x1024"
  }
  ```

  ## Error Responses

  ### 400 Bad Request
  - Invalid model ID
  - Unsupported image format (e.g., AVIF)
  - Invalid aspect ratio
  - Too many reference images for model

  ### 401 Unauthorized
  - Missing or invalid API key

  ### 402 Payment Required
  - Insufficient credits

  ## Rate Limits
  - Varies by plan
  - Check response headers for rate limit info
}
